1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:08,842
I wonder where everyone meets
their soulmates.

2
00:00:08,925 --> 00:00:13,138
I want a rich, handsome husband too.

3
00:00:13,221 --> 00:00:16,182
The new season of <i>Last Princess</i>
is streaming!

4
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:17,809
All right, let’s watch it! Right now!

5
00:00:17,892 --> 00:00:20,687
I'm in the mood for romance,
so we are watching this now!

6
00:00:21,312 --> 00:00:23,106
I'm Kotaro Komiyama.

7
00:00:23,189 --> 00:00:24,107
<i>Through my hobby,</i>

8
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:26,985
<i>I've built up some muscles.</i>
<i>That's my charm.</i>

9
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:29,362
This guy seems super shady.

10
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:31,114
Total meathead vibes.

11
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:32,282
<i>I'm Airi.</i>

12
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:36,161
I'm 27 years old. I work as a model.

13
00:00:36,244 --> 00:00:37,787
Wow, she's gorgeous!

14
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:40,040
She's totally a pro at this romance stuff.

15
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:41,458
She's not all that.

16
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:43,168
-Wow, you're amazing!
-Not really.

17
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:45,044
Saunas are very trendy right now.

18
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:47,172
They are, they're super popular.

19
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:49,758
You're such a sharp businessman
to see opportunity in that!

20
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:53,386
There it is!
Those are staple lines of popular girls.

21
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:54,929
-"You're amazing!"
-"I didn't know that!"

22
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,306
-"Wow!"
-"You have great sense!"

23
00:00:56,389 --> 00:00:57,599
"I see."

24
00:00:57,682 --> 00:00:59,976
You two are amazing!

25
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,479
I went and got certified
as a food advisor!

26
00:01:02,562 --> 00:01:04,939
<i>-Really?</i>
-Oh, she has qualifications.

27
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:06,483
So she's not like me.

28
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:08,985
I like people who are like aliens.

29
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:11,071
There it is, the quirky ditz persona.

30
00:01:11,154 --> 00:01:14,157
When you can't win with a conventional
approach, you have to act weird.

31
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,534
Girls like her surprisingly
make it far in these shows.

32
00:01:16,618 --> 00:01:19,537
I want to have a romance
like <i>Last Princess </i>too!

33
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:23,291
Who are you?

34
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:26,753
Mr. Konta invited us over!

35
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:30,131
Isn't this just like…

36
00:01:30,215 --> 00:01:32,175
Our very own reality dating show?

37
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:34,177
-I've got to put on makeup.
-What?

38
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:36,596
-Me too!
-Huh? Wait… Well…

39
00:01:37,305 --> 00:01:39,557
Please wait just a moment.

40
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:42,477
I have no choice but to win.

41
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:44,062
I am confident.

42
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:48,650
I'm betting my 27 years of life,
I will win this.

43
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:52,737
<i>I want to be in a relationship</i>
<i>where we help each other grow.</i>

44
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:55,198
And I will find it, no matter what.

45
00:01:56,157 --> 00:02:01,913
<i>Who will win and be chosen</i>
<i>as the last princess?</i>

46
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:07,418
Okay…

47
00:02:08,795 --> 00:02:11,798
Whoa. So much trash.

48
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:24,811
-Here.
-Thank you.

49
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:30,692
So, you all came here
because my brother invited you?

50
00:02:30,775 --> 00:02:32,235
Yes. Wait, he's your brother?

51
00:02:32,318 --> 00:02:33,736
Oh, right.

52
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:36,406
I'm Midori, Konta's younger sister.

53
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:38,950
I'm Rinrin, Midori's friend.

54
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:41,119
Likewise, I'm her friend, Tsumugi.

55
00:02:41,202 --> 00:02:43,580
Sorry, I forgot to introduce myself.
I'm Kotaro.

56
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:45,123
They are my friends from college.

57
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:46,040
I'm Ryusei.

58
00:02:46,124 --> 00:02:46,958
I'm Norito.

59
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:49,210
We came here from Tokyo.

60
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:51,546
We met Mr. Konta by chance
at a roadside station,

61
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:54,507
and he said, "We're having a barbecue
at my villa, you should come."

62
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:55,633
I see.

63
00:02:56,384 --> 00:02:57,969
So, where is my brother?

64
00:02:58,052 --> 00:02:59,721
He's still out buying groceries.

65
00:02:59,804 --> 00:03:02,557
He said, "There are three ladies
at home, you can go there first."

66
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:05,602
Nice, Konta!

67
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:07,520
He can be useful sometimes.

68
00:03:08,897 --> 00:03:13,109
You said you all came from Tokyo,
so what do you do for work?

69
00:03:13,192 --> 00:03:15,486
I work at an IT company.

70
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:17,155
I'm a financial planner.

71
00:03:17,238 --> 00:03:18,740
I run my own company.

72
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,785
They're handsome and successful!

73
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:25,580
Perhaps they are
our matches made in heaven?

74
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:27,874
Our inspirational <i>Last Princess</i>?

75
00:03:27,957 --> 00:03:30,418
Our dating show has finally begun!

76
00:03:54,525 --> 00:03:55,735
That's right.

77
00:03:55,818 --> 00:03:58,780
I think I've been in more relationships
than the average girl.

78
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:03,826
<i>But I think it's about time</i>
<i>I find that one special soulmate.</i>

79
00:04:04,702 --> 00:04:05,536
<i>My type?</i>

80
00:04:06,204 --> 00:04:08,164
Let's see…

81
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:10,792
I think I like a man who can lead,

82
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:13,795
so I can always walk
three steps behind him.

83
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:16,798
I'm actually quite traditional.

84
00:04:18,132 --> 00:04:22,595
RINRIN
#I WILL STOP BEING EVERYONE'S IDOL

85
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:26,391
I came here to experience
the passionate love of a lifetime.

86
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:29,060
WHAT KIND OF LOVE DO YOU WANT?

87
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:30,395
<i>Let's see…</i>

88
00:04:30,478 --> 00:04:35,483
Whether you're my friend or not,
I don't plan on holding back.

89
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:41,614
TSUMUGI
#THE ROMANCE WRECKER WITH NOTHING TO LOSE

90
00:04:42,198 --> 00:04:44,784
I'm currently unemployed.

91
00:04:45,451 --> 00:04:49,455
<i>But when it comes to housework</i>
<i>like cooking and cleaning,</i>

92
00:04:50,164 --> 00:04:52,083
I work harder than anyone!

93
00:04:52,709 --> 00:04:57,130
MIDORI
#MY NEXT WORKPLACE IS Y-O-U!

94
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:59,173
FINALLY, A WORD ON YOUR RESOLVE

95
00:04:59,257 --> 00:05:00,466
-I will…
-Definitely…

96
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:03,803
Find a good person here
and go back to Tokyo with him!

97
00:05:35,543 --> 00:05:38,379
Well then,
here's to our wonderful meeting.

98
00:05:38,921 --> 00:05:42,008
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

99
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:49,640
Drinking at midday,
on a sunny day like this, is the best.

100
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:52,018
It really makes you feel free, doesn't it?

101
00:05:52,101 --> 00:05:53,978
Mr. Kotaro, this is a bit sudden,

102
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:55,813
but can I take a photo
with you over there?

103
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:56,731
Sure.

104
00:05:56,814 --> 00:05:57,732
Thank you.

105
00:06:01,527 --> 00:06:05,281
Rinrin is amazing. She knows that
the first move is crucial in romance.

106
00:06:05,364 --> 00:06:08,534
Right. We can't match her.

107
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:09,660
-Mr. Ryusei.
-What?

108
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:13,372
Care to share some wine
with me over there?

109
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:14,665
Seriously?

110
00:06:14,749 --> 00:06:16,084
Sounds good.

111
00:06:17,126 --> 00:06:18,127
Midori.

112
00:06:18,211 --> 00:06:21,047
Romance is a survival game.

113
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:24,383
Were you always
this motivated about romance?

114
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:42,485
What do you do at your IT company?

115
00:06:42,568 --> 00:06:44,320
I'm the CD for our product branch.

116
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:45,947
CD?

117
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:48,783
Do you mean a CD for listening to music?

118
00:06:48,866 --> 00:06:49,867
<i>Oh, wow!</i>

119
00:06:49,951 --> 00:06:51,619
<i>She's doing the quirky ditz act!</i>

120
00:06:51,702 --> 00:06:54,747
No, that's not it.
It stands for "creative director."

121
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,958
Wow! Creative?

122
00:06:57,041 --> 00:06:59,627
Your job must take a lot of talent!

123
00:06:59,710 --> 00:07:03,297
I'm lucky my tastes are so well-received.

124
00:07:03,381 --> 00:07:04,257
It's just luck.

125
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:07,927
-No, you're talented.
-Not at all.

126
00:07:08,010 --> 00:07:10,847
<i>The popular girls' staple lines…</i>

127
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:13,182
<i>She's making full use of them!</i>

128
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:17,311
By the way, you look pretty well-built.

129
00:07:17,395 --> 00:07:18,855
-You noticed?
-Yes.

130
00:07:18,938 --> 00:07:20,982
Actually, I hit the gym four times a week.

131
00:07:21,065 --> 00:07:24,277
Amazing! Do you also
pay close attention to your diet?

132
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:25,236
I do.

133
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:28,823
My diet basically revolves around
protein and lean meats.

134
00:07:28,906 --> 00:07:31,200
I'm also quite health-conscious.

135
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:34,370
Lately, I even got
a food advisor certificate!

136
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:36,038
-Oh, really?
<i>-Liar!</i>

137
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:38,624
<i>You just saw that on </i>Last Princess!

138
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:40,042
I can make any dish!

139
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:42,795
You're a financial planner, right?

140
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:47,133
Yes. If you're interested,
I can help you with your life planning.

141
00:07:47,216 --> 00:07:48,676
Thank you.

142
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:53,264
Then, in return,
I'll help you with your life planning.

143
00:07:53,347 --> 00:07:56,058
What? Are you also a licensed FP?

144
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:57,977
No, I'm not certified, but…

145
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:00,563
I can see the future.

146
00:08:00,646 --> 00:08:02,773
<i>She's going for the eccentric act!</i>

147
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:04,775
Can you explain?

148
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:06,319
I love fortune-telling.

149
00:08:06,402 --> 00:08:09,655
I do tarot, and I can also read palms.

150
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:11,115
I see!

151
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:12,867
Let me borrow your right hand.

152
00:08:14,535 --> 00:08:16,787
<i>Casual physical contact…</i>

153
00:08:16,871 --> 00:08:20,583
<i>Tsumugi, you are also</i>
<i>quite experienced in this, huh?</i>

154
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:24,962
I've heard celebrities and successful
people often have a "charisma line."

155
00:08:25,046 --> 00:08:26,464
Do I have it?

156
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:31,135
No, it doesn't look like
you have a charisma line.

157
00:08:31,719 --> 00:08:34,347
However, your life line
is incredibly long.

158
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:38,768
Oh, and your head line is quite short.

159
00:08:38,851 --> 00:08:39,852
Short?

160
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,062
Wait, do you even have it?

161
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:42,021
Maybe you don't.

162
00:08:42,104 --> 00:08:44,774
-Can you cook anything?
-Oh, that's not it.

163
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:48,694
What kind of work do you do?

164
00:08:49,445 --> 00:08:50,279
Oh.

165
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:54,033
I am not working right now.

166
00:08:54,116 --> 00:08:56,244
A lot happened.

167
00:08:56,327 --> 00:09:00,373
You're Mr. Konta's younger sister, right?

168
00:09:00,456 --> 00:09:01,290
Yes.

169
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:03,751
I see! That explains it!

170
00:09:03,834 --> 00:09:05,920
What? No, that's not it!

171
00:09:06,003 --> 00:09:09,298
You see, unlike my brother,
I actually care about my future.

172
00:09:09,382 --> 00:09:11,175
-It's okay, I understand.
-What?

173
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:13,344
-I'm the same way.
-What?

174
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:16,722
What kind of business
are you preparing to launch?

175
00:09:16,806 --> 00:09:18,891
B-Business?

176
00:09:18,975 --> 00:09:21,602
Well, I'm not sure about business.

177
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:24,939
In fact, I'm not even sure
what I want to do yet.

178
00:09:25,022 --> 00:09:26,357
-Ms. Midori!
-What?

179
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:28,109
That is a dangerous way of thinking.

180
00:09:28,192 --> 00:09:29,026
What?

181
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:33,364
If you think of business in terms of
what you want to do, you will fail!

182
00:09:34,031 --> 00:09:34,865
No, but…

183
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:37,034
I don't plan to start a business.

184
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:38,035
What?

185
00:09:41,122 --> 00:09:43,082
Oh, well…

186
00:09:43,165 --> 00:09:45,626
How do I start, then?

187
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:47,128
First is surveying.

188
00:09:47,211 --> 00:09:50,840
You survey various people
to identify insights before you set up.

189
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:53,926
There are so many entrepreneurs
who don't understand this.

190
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:55,761
That's why everyone fails.

191
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:59,849
I see. You're amazing, Mr. Norito.

192
00:09:59,932 --> 00:10:01,892
Oh, if you would like,

193
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:05,146
I have a members-only service
where I post all about entrepreneurship.

194
00:10:05,229 --> 00:10:07,148
Would you like to subscribe to my service?

195
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:08,149
A subscription?

196
00:10:08,232 --> 00:10:12,612
Yes! You can learn business know-how
for just 550 yen a month.

197
00:10:12,695 --> 00:10:13,613
It's a great deal.

198
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:19,243
<i>Subscribe?</i>

199
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:21,412
No, I won't.

200
00:10:21,495 --> 00:10:24,165
I can't afford
to be wasting money right now.

201
00:10:24,665 --> 00:10:28,085
I was thinking when I eventually
get married and have a family,

202
00:10:28,169 --> 00:10:30,087
for the sake of my children,

203
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:34,133
I should acquire some knowledge
about food and cooking, starting now.

204
00:10:34,216 --> 00:10:37,136
Wait, am I getting ahead of myself?

205
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:47,313
I'm sorry, did I talk too much?

206
00:10:48,939 --> 00:10:52,026
No, it's just… too dazzling.

207
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:54,153
Oh, my…

208
00:10:55,488 --> 00:10:56,739
I mean the sunlight.

209
00:10:57,281 --> 00:10:58,240
What?

210
00:10:59,325 --> 00:11:01,494
I really don't want to get a sunburn.

211
00:11:01,577 --> 00:11:03,162
Could we swap seats?

212
00:11:03,245 --> 00:11:05,081
Actually, should we just head inside?

213
00:11:06,332 --> 00:11:07,667
Should we do that?

214
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,460
-Let's go inside.
-Yeah.

215
00:11:09,543 --> 00:11:11,545
<i>If you hate UV rays that much,</i>

216
00:11:11,629 --> 00:11:14,757
you should have worn sunscreen
before coming!

217
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:18,636
This painting
must be really expensive too.

218
00:11:18,719 --> 00:11:19,887
That's true.

219
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:21,013
It's amazing, right?

220
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:22,807
Yes, it has a deep flavor.

221
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:24,809
A deep flavor?

222
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:26,352
All right!

223
00:11:26,435 --> 00:11:27,728
So heavy.

224
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:30,022
I'm back!

225
00:11:32,566 --> 00:11:34,318
-Are you a guest?
-Right.

226
00:11:34,402 --> 00:11:35,444
He's our servant.

227
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:36,529
I see.

228
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:37,530
Nice to meet you.

229
00:11:37,613 --> 00:11:39,198
Oh, hello.

230
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,994
Amazing.

231
00:11:54,046 --> 00:11:55,464
What would you like to drink next?

232
00:11:57,049 --> 00:11:58,592
I'm not sure…

233
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:00,845
Hey.

234
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:03,222
Do you have red? Red?

235
00:12:03,931 --> 00:12:04,765
Red?

236
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:06,392
I mean red wine.

237
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:10,354
-Oh, red!
-Red wine. Yes, please.

238
00:12:11,439 --> 00:12:12,940
Red…

239
00:12:13,023 --> 00:12:15,151
-Oh, red!
-It's beautiful.

240
00:12:16,402 --> 00:12:19,363
-It's a great size.
-That's right.

241
00:12:19,447 --> 00:12:20,322
Red.

242
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:23,576
-The walls are pretty too.
-Yes, they are.

243
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:25,494
-They go well together.
-Yes.

244
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:29,707
Red!

245
00:12:30,624 --> 00:12:31,792
Wait, no.

246
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:32,793
That's a lot.

247
00:12:33,961 --> 00:12:35,296
Oh, wow.

248
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,173
Well then!

249
00:12:37,256 --> 00:12:39,091
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

250
00:12:42,344 --> 00:12:43,929
This color…

251
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:46,515
I wonder if it's a Pinot Noir
from Burgundy.

252
00:12:56,692 --> 00:12:57,943
Cherry…

253
00:12:58,027 --> 00:13:00,070
Raspberry… It's so fruity.

254
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:01,197
RED WINE FOR COOKING USE

255
00:13:02,907 --> 00:13:04,992
But the mouthfeel is soft.

256
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:08,120
SUPER CHEAP RED WINE FOR COOKING USE

257
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:10,247
Hey, this isn't bad.

258
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:13,834
I think if you decant it a bit more,
the aroma will open up even further.

259
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:15,920
Decant?

260
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:17,296
Decant. This.

261
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:20,299
Decant?

262
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,553
-Decant.
-Decant!

263
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:28,599
That wine is a cooking wine
I bought from a nearby supermarket.

264
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:30,559
A 780-yen wine.

265
00:13:32,269 --> 00:13:34,355
Was there anyone you liked?

266
00:13:34,438 --> 00:13:39,568
Let's see… How should I put it?
It's not that they're bad people…

267
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:40,861
I get it.

268
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:43,697
It's like…

269
00:13:43,781 --> 00:13:47,159
They are completely empty inside.

270
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:48,494
Exactly.

271
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:53,791
They sound smart when they talk,
but they feel weirdly shallow.

272
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:56,168
It seems they were classmates in college.

273
00:13:56,252 --> 00:13:57,753
He gave me his socials.

274
00:13:58,879 --> 00:13:59,755
Wow!

275
00:13:59,838 --> 00:14:02,174
It feels like a seminar channel!

276
00:14:03,259 --> 00:14:06,262
Well, it's not like
they're bad people, right?

277
00:14:06,345 --> 00:14:08,389
I'm going to stick it out a little longer!

278
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:09,848
I've had enough.

279
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:12,268
Seminar guys
are not romantic options for me.

280
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:13,185
True.

281
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:15,312
When I talked to him,
he was all business talk.

282
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:16,480
What is up with that?

283
00:14:23,529 --> 00:14:25,489
Would you like a refill?

284
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:26,699
Thank you.

285
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:31,704
By the way, do you all have girlfriends?

286
00:14:31,787 --> 00:14:33,080
No, I don't.

287
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:34,540
-Me neither.
-Same here.

288
00:14:34,623 --> 00:14:37,251
Oh! I thought girls
would be all over you guys!

289
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:38,502
No way.

290
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:41,839
I guess work is my girlfriend right now.

291
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:44,967
My marriage phase
is quite far in the future.

292
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:49,430
Hey, will Mr. Konta be back soon?

293
00:14:49,513 --> 00:14:51,515
I got a message from him earlier.

294
00:14:51,599 --> 00:14:53,100
He said he'll be here any minute.

295
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:55,019
I see! Great!

296
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:58,063
We came here
because we wanted to talk to him!

297
00:14:58,147 --> 00:14:59,023
What?

298
00:14:59,106 --> 00:15:02,735
Mr. Konta, the millionaire
who got to retire at a young age.

299
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:05,821
Say what?

300
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:27,092
What made you so interested in me?

301
00:15:27,176 --> 00:15:29,094
I knew you were someone extraordinary!

302
00:15:29,178 --> 00:15:31,972
<i>Please teach us the secret</i>
<i>to your success, Mr. Konta.</i>

303
00:15:32,056 --> 00:15:33,724
<i>How you became a millionaire</i>
<i>at a young age!</i>

304
00:15:33,807 --> 00:15:35,976
<i>The three of us</i>
<i>actually post videos online.</i>

305
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:38,437
<i>Would you consider appearing in one?</i>

306
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:39,480
<i>Cheers!</i>

307
00:15:39,563 --> 00:15:40,564
No! The meat!

308
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:46,236
<i>Today, I think I finally figured out</i>
<i>who I should really be looking at.</i>

309
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,696
Would you be willing to invest in us?

310
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:48,697
1,000.

311
00:15:48,781 --> 00:15:49,657
Sure.

312
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:50,699
Mr. Nishigami!

313
00:15:50,783 --> 00:15:53,369
I am… Mr. Nishigami…

314
00:15:58,582 --> 00:15:59,625
What?

315
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:01,502
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
